From 9dc7e40962f11d1d9a5568f8a7633a695288329c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:40:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bearer: Remove disconn_timer when freeing the bearer

The timer armed by Disconnect is only removed when it fires or when the
bearer disconnects, so a device removed within DISCONNECT_TIMER seconds of
a Disconnect call leaves it to run bearer_disconnect_link() on the freed
bearer.

Remove it in bearer_free().

Fixes: 4e21ebcaa5d0 ("bearer: Implement Connect/Disconnect methods")
Assisted-by: OpenCode:claude-opus-5.5
---
 src/bearer.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/bearer.c b/src/bearer.c
index 5544c2f..ea3bf69 100644
--- a/src/bearer.c
+++ b/src/bearer.c
@@ -67,6 +67,9 @@ static void bearer_free(void *data)
 {
 	struct btd_bearer *bearer = data;
 
+	if (bearer->disconn_timer)
+		timeout_remove(bearer->disconn_timer);
+
 	free(bearer);
 }
 
